BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Quiet Light: Watercolor Basics  — Sebastopol Center For the Arts
 \, California
DTSTART:20261107T000000
DTEND:20261108T000000
UID:c104d4eea042c90eb0cd3e8fe819864e@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Out of Stock\n      \n    \n\n\n\n\n\nQuiet Light: Watercolor 
 Basics\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $170.00\n        \n      \
 n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, November 7th\, 2026 10AM - 4PMSettle into the quie
 t beauty of late fall with a day of watercolor inspired bySonoma County in
  November—natural forms gathered from the season—pomegranates\, mushro
 oms\, lichen\, branches\, turning leaves\, seed pods\,and olives all broug
 ht into the classroom for observation and inspiration.The focus is on the 
 contrast of rich\, saturated color and varied texture—fiery maples\, gol
 ds\, and russets alongside muted stems\, weathered bark\,and softer\, fadi
 ng tones.Learn basic watercolor techniques including wet-on-wet painting\,
  controlledwashes\, layering\, color mixing\, and creating texture\, while
  building strongcompositions using color\, light\, and form. Guided discus
 sions explore theessential elements of visual art to help you create expre
 ssive\, individualwork.All materials provided. Space limited to 12 student
 s.Discussion break at 12:30 p.m. Please bring a brown bag lunch.About the 
 Instructor: Lynn Zachreson studied art at the University of Minnesota and 
 San Jose State University—Painting\, Printmaking: BA Fine Art. She has e
 xperience teaching all ages: Watercolor painting skills\, 30+ years\, Wate
 rcolor figure painting 20+ years\, and Fine Art Basics with Mixed Media 20
 + years. Lynn enjoys spending her time painting\, teaching\, long distance
  hiking\, and gardening. View Lynn’s art here: https://lynnzachresonart.
 com/\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            Reserve Your Spot
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/quiet-light-watercolor-basics
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Returning to the First Mark with Catherine Cruz - November 7th —
  Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20261107T000000
DTEND:20261108T000000
UID:b24cf8c2cda9a8626fbad83f261f0506@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Returning to the First Mark with Catherine Cruz - November 7th
 \n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $130.00\n        \n      \n    \
 n  \n\nReturning to the First Mark November 7th\, 2026 - 11:00am-3:00pm At
 tendance Price: $130.00 Ages 16+In this new workshop we will explore drawi
 ng and abstract mark making through play\, curiosity\, and child-like wond
 er.Before we learned to write words\, we communicated through marks. As ch
 ildren\, we drew with curiosity\, freedom\, and a sense of play - without 
 worrying about getting it "right” and without fear of getting our hands 
 dirty.  We played in the dirt and we made things.  This workshop invites
  you to reconnect with that creative spirit through abstract mark making a
 nd intuitive drawing.Using a variety of drawing tools and materials\, we'l
 l explore line\, texture\, rhythm\, and gesture as a personal visual langu
 age. Through guided exercises and playful experimentation\, you'll discove
 r how letting go of expectations can open the door to greater creativity a
 nd self-expression.Whether you're an experienced artist or simply curious 
 about abstract drawing\, you'll leave with new techniques\, greater confid
 ence\, and a renewed sense of creative freedom. No drawing experience is n
 ecessary - just a willingness to explore.When our drawings are complete we
  will assemble and collage them to create a scroll!Returning to the first 
 mark means:→ reconnecting with curiosity→ slowing down and truly seein
 g→ discovering the language within ordinary things→ responding intuiti
 vely→ building something personal through lines and marksParticipant mus
 t bring the following:Note: There is no need to buy expensive materials\, 
 please consider what you already have.  If you’re missing something\, l
 et the instructor know\, Sebastopol Center for the Arts has a minimal amou
 nt of these supplies available to borrow.Apron or clothing you don't mind 
 getting paint onBlack gesso or black acrylic paintSpray bottle with water 
 Acrylic paint: two or three earthy colors such as burnt umber\, raw sienna
 \, or yellow ochre.  If you don’t have these specific colors\, no need 
 to purchase them\, just bring whatever you haveA small container\, like a 
 glass jar\, to pour the gesso inA variety of paint brushes (3 to 5) from v
 ery thin to thickA container for waterDifferent types of paper to draw on\
 , from small to large sheets.  Examples: recycled book pages\, copy paper
 \, drawing pad\, newsprint\, brown paper bags\, vintage papers with or wit
 hout illustrations but nothing too dark or too busy. Two black pens or ma
 rkers with different tipsGlue stickScissorsPaper towelsThe class will begi
 n with a talk and a demonstration\, so please plan to arrive early to allo
 w time to settle in.A short lunch break will be held from 12:30 to 1:00 PM
 . Kindly bring your own lunch and beverage.About the instructor: Catherine
  Cruz is a French-American artist whose work is informed by textures and p
 atterns created by the passing of time and the effects of the natural elem
 ents on the built environment. She holds a Bachelor of Science in interior
  design and she worked in the field of architectural design and green buil
 ding certification for over 25 years. She has taught collage and mixed med
 ia workshops in the Bay Area and in France since 2019\, and this is her fi
 fth year at the Sebastopol Center for the Arts. Her studio is located in S
 ebastopol and she participates in Art Trails Open Studios. You may contact
  Catherine at beyouartstudio@gmail.com. Check out Catherine’s other clas
 ses here: https://wwws.sebarts.org/visual-arts-classes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n 
              \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/returning-to-the-first-mark-w
 ith-catherine-cruz-november-7th
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Still Life in Acrylic  — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, Califo
 rnia
DTSTART:20261108T000000
DTEND:20261109T000000
UID:3f1934dea6a122dc35c90f821c0f108e@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Still Life in Acrylic\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n         
  $67.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nStill Life in Acrylic Date: Sunday\
 , November 8th\, 2026Time: 10:00am-2:00pm Where: Sebastopol Center for the
  Arts is located at 282 South High Street in Sebastopol\, CA. Details rega
 rding class room and directions will be sent to students 24 hours before t
 he class beings. Price: $67.00 Attendance Price Students: This class is re
 stricted to a maximum of 12 students. Register while you can! If this clas
 s is sold out\, please click where it says ‘sold out’  to join the wai
 tlist! Class Description: In this introductory class\, you will learn basi
 c painting techniques of composition\, value blocking\, and color mixing. 
 Students will be creating a single still life on canvas from start to fini
 sh\, painting objects selected by the instructor. Students will learn to o
 bserve shapes and their relationship to space\, utilize tone and color to 
 demonstrate depth\, light\, and shadow\, and how to complete an acrylic pa
 inting. This class is perfect for beginners\, and painters of all skill-l
 evels\, looking to hone in their acrylic painting skills. This class uses
  donated materials to help support our arts education program and provide 
 cost-friendly\, accessible\, classes! About the Teacher: Ayla Carls is a m
 ultidisciplinary artist in the Bay Area\, with interest in acrylic paintin
 g\, oil pastels\, photography\, print making\, stain glass\, and more! Ayl
 a graduated from the University of SanFrancisco and holds a degree in desi
 gn and fine arts. Ayla has been painting for as long as she can remember\,
  and uses her art practice to connect with herself and her experience in t
 he world around her. Ayla’s practice focuses on capturing the joys aroun
 d us in everyday life\, with the goal of bringing joy to others through ar
 t and creating. Learn more about Ayla on her website here. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n          
