DESCRIPTION:Eco Petals: Crafting a Recycled Bouquet (11/14/2026)\n\n  \n  
   \n      \n        \n          $70.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSatu
 rday\, November 14th\, 1:00-4:00pm$60 + $10 Materials feeAges 13+Create a 
 whimsical upcycled bouquet using imagination and an assortment of found an
 d recycled papers. In this playful workshop\, you’ll learn simple techni
 ques for shaping paper flowers and combining colors\, textures\, and unexp
 ected materials. No experience needed—just come ready to explore and lea
 ve with a one-of-a-kind handmade bouquet. All supplies provided.About the 
 Instructor: Rendell Hourigan received a BBA in Marketing from Texas Tech U
 niversity\, and has pursued art for over 25 years\, focusing on sustainabl
 e mixed media. She has studied with artists including Chery Baird\, Jenny 
 London\, and Teri Sloat\, exploring drawing\, collage\, and soft pastels. 
 Her training includes workshops and courses in art journaling\, mosaics\, 
 and mark-making. She’s exhibited work at the Sebastopol Center for the A
 rts\, The Graton Gallery\, and her SOFA district studio. Drawn to the beau
 ty of discarded materials and passionate about recycling\, she incorporate
 s reclaimed materials into her work and now leads art workshops to inspire
  eco-conscious creativity in others.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
