SUMMARY:Poetry Lives in November 2026  — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\
 , California
DTSTART:20261124T000000
DTEND:20261125T000000
UID:4fad940b6502303949c88f90d2e17a41@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Poetry Lives! November 24th!\n\n  \n    \n      \n      from $
 0.00\n    \n  \n\nEvery Fourth Tuesday: November 24th\, 2026 6:00-7:00pm: 
 Spoken Word Workshop 7:15-8:30pm: Open Mic Open to All$5/10/15/20 Sliding 
 Scale for Workshop Join us for an evening of spoken word poetry here at th
 e Sebastopol Center for the Arts! Students of all walks of life\, abilitie
 s\, and experience writing poetry\, or spoken word poetry\, are encouraged
  to join. Students will engage in a freewrite\, poetry reading\, discussio
 n\, and structured writing with a voluntary shareout. After the one hour w
 orkshop\, Poetry Lives! will act as an Open Mic night open to all to read 
 their completed\, or previously completed\, poems. To register for the Op
 en Mic only\, please select Open Mic Only below! All workshop registration
 s include registration to the open mic as well. Poetry Lives! is a monthly
  poetry workshop and open mic series that aims to create a space for anyon
 e and everyone to come\, learn more about poetic craft\, and share their p
 oetry. The event starts with a facilitated hour-long workshop dedicated to
  learning craft elements\, discovering new poets\, and generating new work
 . Once the workshop concludes\, we will hold a hosted open mic for anyone 
 who wishes to share. It is not mandatory to participate in the workshop to
  be a part of the open mic or vice versa. This event is all ages\, but tha
 t doesn't necessarily mean family-friendly\, as poets are known to cover m
 ature and adult topics from time to time. About the Poet: Jordan Ranft (H
 e/Him) is a writer and therapist from Northern California. He has been nom
 inated for a Pushcart and Best of the Net. His poetry has been published o
 r is forthcoming in Boulevard Magazine\, Frontier Poetry\, Poetry Online\,
  Bear Review\, Iron Horse Literary Review\, and elsewhere. His first chapb
 ook\, Said the Worms\, was published in June 2023 by Wrong Publishing. He 
 is currently working on a second chapbook and full-length collection. Inst
 agram: @Jordan_Ranft // @poetrylivessonoma\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                
   Workshop:\n                \n\n\n\n                      Select Workshop
 \n                    \n$5.00\n$10.00\n$15.00\n$20.00\nOpen Mic Only\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
