BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Asemic Writing — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\
 , California
DTSTART:20261212T000000
DTEND:20261213T000000
UID:00c6d7e8985a23a860f9fa261b5b1491@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Introduction to Asemic Writing (December 12th)\n\n  \n    \n  
     \n        \n          $175.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nIntroduct
 ion to Asemic Writing Saturday\, December 12th\, 2026 - 10:00am-4:00pm$160
 .00 + $15.00 Materials Fee = $175.00 RegistrationClass Limited to 12 Stude
 ntsRegister now for both of Sherrie Lovler’s Workshops this weekend\, an
 d receive $20.00 off your total order! Use code SHRRLVLR-EARLYBIRD-1212132
 6 until November 12th to claim your discount!December 12th: Introduction t
 o Asemic WritingDecember 13th: Wabi-Sabi Ink Painting: Finding Beauty in I
 mperfectionClass Description: Asemic writing is the creation of marks that
  resemble handwriting but carry no literal meaning or readable text. It is
  the word before words form—the voice too distant to be understood—a u
 niversal expression without country or dialect.We’ll begin with a slides
 how exploring the rich history and possibilities of asemic writing\, from 
 ancient scripts and symbols to the calligraphic line and the work of conte
 mporary artists. From there\, you’ll begin your own exploration using in
 k\, watercolor\, and a variety of tools on paper.Through guided exercises 
 and playful experimentation\, we’ll explore line\, gesture\, rhythm\, re
 petition\, and space. You’ll discover how asemic marks can infiltrate an
 d transform your existing artwork or become works of art in their own righ
 t.You’ll leave with a collection of new work\, fresh approaches to mark-
 making\, and a deeper trust in your own intuition and expressive voice. My
  intention is to guide you beyond casual scribbling toward authentic marks
 —marks that arise from the heart and become uniquely your own.All levels
  welcome.IMPORTANT: CLICK HERE FOR THE LIST OF REQUIRED MATERIALS FOR THIS
  CLASS. Not all materials are provided\, please see the list of request ma
 terials above. If you have any questions regarding materials\, please cont
 act your instructor: sherrie@artandpoetry.com—About the Instructor: Sher
 rie Lovler is a painter\, poet\, and teacher whose work bridges Western ca
 lligraphy and the expressive spirit of Asian brush painting. With a BA in 
 Studio Art\, she has taught for several decades at international calligrap
 hy conferences and institutions including Ghost Ranch\, Northern Arizona U
 niversity\, and local art centers. Her paintings explore the space between
  writing and image. Inspired by Asian brushwork and the Japanese aesthetic
  of wabi-sabi\, she embraces imperfection\, spontaneity\, and fluid mark-m
 aking. Sumi ink\, gesture\, color\, and asemic writing become an abstract 
 visual language. She is the author\, illustrator\, and designer of the awa
 rd-winning book On Softer Ground. Her latest book\, Distant Voices\, explo
 res art as a collaboration with nature\, poetry\, and unseen influences. S
 he participates in Sonoma County Art Trails\, Art at the Source\, and pres
 ented a solo exhibition at Gallery Route One in Point Reyes Station in 202
 5. www.artandpoetry.com\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n              \n                A
 dd to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/introduction-to-asemic-writin
 g
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Explore Gel Plate Printing - December 12th — Sebastopol Center F
 or the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20261212T000000
DTEND:20261213T000000
UID:380edbe359475c5ddb3623fc48dbbe82@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Explore Gel Plate Printing - December 12th\n\n  \n    \n      
 \n        \n          $130.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, De
 cember 12th\, 2026\; 11 AM – 3 PMFee: $115 + $15 materials feeAge: 16+ E
 xplore the art of gel plate printing with French-American artist Catherine
  Cruz. You will learn to create beautiful monoprint designs on paper using
  a gel plate and acrylic paint. You will take home lots of prints that can
  be used for creating collage\, mixed media art or greeting cards. This cl
 ass is perfect for anyone wanting to learn this unique monoprint style and
  is perfect for beginners.The instructor will teach you the basic skills f
 or using this fun tool\, from printing textural backgrounds\, to layering 
 colors and using a variety of unexpected tools.Note: Image transfer techni
 que is not part of this class.What you will learn: Methods for applying pa
 int and pulling successful printsTechniques for creating intricate layered
  designsCreative use of mark-making tools and masksStrategies for combinin
 g techniquesThe instructor will provide a gel plate\, brayer\, acrylic pai
 nt and mark-making tools. A variety of papers will be provided but we enco
 urage you to bring your own papers to experiment with.Click below for Mate
 rials ListIMPORTANT: Instructions for where to purchase your materials and
  how to prepare them is provided in the attached PDF. The instructor will 
 start the class with a demonstration so please arrive a few minutes early 
 to get set up so we can start on time.  We will take a short break for lun
 ch between 12:30 and 1:00 pm so bring your lunch and a beverage.   About t
 he instructor: Catherine Cruz is a French-American artist whose work is in
 formed by textures and patterns created by the passing of time and the eff
 ects of the natural elements on the built environment.  She holds a Bachel
 or of Science in interior design and she worked in the field of architectu
 ral design and green building certification for over 25 years.  She has ta
 ught collage and mixed media workshops in the Bay Area and in France since
  2019\, and this is her fifth year at the Sebastopol Center for the Arts. 
  Her studio is located in Sebastopol and she participates in Art Trails Op
 en Studios.  You may contact Catherine at beyouartstudio@gmail.com.  Check
  out Catherine’s other classes here:  https://wwws.sebarts.org/visual-ar
 ts-classes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
